281
00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.300
<v Maya>aiming for $64.3 billion.

282
00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:38.640
<v Alex>That’s a big leap.

283
00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.620
<v Maya>They also project a valuation up to $1.4 trillion.

284
00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.820
<v Alex>So the IPO is a big deal.

285
00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:50.060
<v Maya>Plus, the White House meeting with Speaker Johnson had tech execs on the table.

286
00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:52.680
<v Maya>This feels like a chess move, not a scramble.

287
00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:58.040
<v Alex>Hold on, what’s the point of a CEO hunt when the market’s already eyeing a

288
00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.360
<v Alex>trillion‑dollar IPO?

289
00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:04.580
<v Maya>I think it signals confidence in AI revenue streams; the timing is just a

290
00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:05.000
<v Maya>coincidence.

291
00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:09.320
<v Alex>I don't buy that; the timing suggests a tug‑of‑war for talent.

292
00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:13.450
<v Maya>The White House meeting shows regulators want to stay ahead,

293
00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.080
<v Maya>so Nvidia’s leadership change could smooth that.

294
00:15:16.567 --> 00:15:20.340
<v Alex>But if Anthropic is pulling $64 billion,

295
00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:23.180
<v Alex>Nvidia’s new CEO might just be a placeholder.

296
00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:28.580
<v Maya>It could be a strategic hedge; keeping Nvidia stable while the IPO plays out.

297
00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:33.860
<v Alex>In short, it’s a sign that the AI race isn’t just tech, it’s a market sprint.

298
00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:38.530
<v Alex>You're listening to First Tick, from Bits and Tickers.

299
00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:40.270
<v Alex>That's about the halfway mark.

300
00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:41.040
<v Alex>Still to come.

301
00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.980
<v Alex>AI debt surges, IMF warns.

302
00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:48.280
<v Alex>Nvidia earnings, a succession drama, and China.

303
00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:51.540
<v Alex>And Uber picks up Amazon’s driverless cars in Vegas.

304
00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:55.340
<v Maya>And if you just joined us, I'm Maya, that's Alex,

305
00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:57.500
<v Maya>and every story is linked in the show notes.

306
00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:03.950
<v Alex>IMF says the AI market is basically a debt‑backed one‑legged stand.

307
00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:08.260
<v Maya>It’s $1 trillion, two‑thirds debt, according to CNBC.

308
00:16:08.652 --> 00:16:09.280
<v Alex>That fast?

309
00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.270
<v Maya>Who’s pulling the strings on that debt?

310
00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:16.420
<v Alex>Investors keep buying AI companies, then sell back through orders, making a loop.

311
00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:22.310
<v Maya>And the risk is that a sudden pullback could knock $50 billion out, UBS notes.

312
00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:27.020
<v Alex>If rates climb and borrowing costs rise, that loop could tighten quickly.

313
00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:31.260
<v Maya>So the market could wobble if confidence dips, IMF warns.

314
00:16:31.903 --> 00:16:35.780
<v Maya>What exactly do you mean by “circular financing” in the AI space?

315
00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:41.240
<v Alex>It’s when money poured into an AI firm ends up flowing back when that firm places

316
00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:46.680
<v Alex>orders with suppliers—so the investor’s cash circles back through the supply chain.

317
00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.660
<v Maya>So it’s not a straight line of funding, it loops back?

318
00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:53.920
<v Alex>And the IMF says that whole loop now totals just over $1 trillion.

319
00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:57.960
<v Maya>Two‑thirds of that is debt—do we know why it’s so leveraged?

320
00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:03.800
<v Alex>Investors are chasing quick returns; debt lets them amplify exposure without

321
00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:05.670
<v Alex>putting more equity on the table.

322
00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.090
<v Maya>But who’s the main debt‑lender in this loop?

323
00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:14.200
<v Alex>The article points to Nvidia’s financing pullback as a big threat—UBS estimates a

324
00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:17.230
<v Alex>$50 billion hit if Nvidia pulls back.

325
00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:22.680
<v Alex>I think the debt loop is a fragile trampoline; one misstep and the whole thing

326
00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:23.960
<v Alex>could bounce out of shape.

327
00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:28.210
<v Maya>Yeah, but the IMF says it’s “orderly” right now,

328
00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.730
<v Maya>so maybe it’s just a shaky platform that’s holding up.

329
00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:35.180
<v Alex>The loop’s already over a trillion—more than a typical startup round.

330
00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:38.220
<v Maya>It’s debt‑heavy, so if the interest rates climb,

331
00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:41.000
<v Maya>the cost of keeping that loop alive spikes.

332
00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:45.060
<v Alex>So the pullback from Nvidia could yank $50 billion?

333
00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:47.220
<v Alex>That’s a lot of debt suddenly gone.

334
00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:52.160
<v Maya>My read is that the market is watching the AI leg; if confidence dips,

335
00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:54.130
<v Maya>the whole supply chain feels it.

336
00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:59.680
<v Alex>It’s like building a house on a single beam; if one bolt loosens, the roof tilts.

337
00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:03.880
<v Maya>So the takeaway is, keep an eye on the debt load—if it wobbles,

338
00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.570
<v Maya>the whole economy might feel the shake.

339
00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:11.580
<v Maya>This earnings report caught my eye because it’s the first one since Jensen Huang

340
00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.920
<v Maya>stepped down, according to CNBC.

341
00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.020
<v Alex>Stepped down?

342
00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:17.870
<v Maya>Yeah, he resigned last Thursday,

343
00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:21.820
<v Maya>and Colette Kress is now interim CEO while they look for a replacement.

344
00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:22.880
<v Alex>Okay, that's new.

345
00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.740
<v Maya>They're expecting significant growth,

346
00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:31.280
<v Maya>still – 91% revenue growth is the current estimate – but the real questions are

347
